WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.353 --> 00:00:17.255
the next morning, the gang left the hideout in the woods.

2
00:00:20.037 --> 00:00:26.281
About noon they reached a village, where they separated because everyone had their own criminal activities to pursue.

3
00:00:27.702 --> 00:00:29.664
Ruffler put Frank in charge of Edward.

4
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.501
Frank pulled Edward by the arm.

5
00:00:33.521 --> 00:00:36.542
"Come on, we've got work to do."

6
00:00:36.562 --> 00:00:39.923
"You have no right to touch the king."

7
00:00:41.244 --> 00:00:45.145
Edward tried to shake off Frank's hand, but the young man held on tightly.

8
00:00:45.165 --> 00:00:50.568
"Just making sure you don't try to run back to your er palace."

9
00:00:51.828 --> 00:00:53.629
Frank flashed an evil grin.

10
00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:01.092
They walked up and down the streets, occasionally stopping to look in shop windows.

11
00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:05.801
"What are you looking for?"

12
00:01:06.281 --> 00:01:06.902
Edward said.

13
00:01:06.922 --> 00:01:09.044
"Something to steal."

14
00:01:09.064 --> 00:01:12.487
"Something to steal?

15
00:01:13.988 --> 00:01:15.809
Oh no, I'm not helping you steal.

16
00:01:15.989 --> 00:01:19.893
It's wrong to—" "Don't worry, crybaby," Frank snapped.

17
00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:23.495
"There's nothing worth stealing in this place.

18
00:01:23.676 --> 00:01:25.057
So we're going to beg."

19
00:01:26.838 --> 00:01:30.921
"We?" Edward was outraged at the suggestion that a king would beg.

20
00:01:30.942 --> 00:01:33.724
"You can beg, but I won't do it."

21
00:01:35.608 --> 00:01:37.329
Frank eyed Edward with surprise.

22
00:01:37.349 --> 00:01:40.430
"Since when have you reformed?"

23
00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:43.090
"What are you talking about?"

24
00:01:43.531 --> 00:01:44.231
Edward asked.

25
00:01:44.251 --> 00:01:49.532
"According to your father, you've spent your whole life begging on the streets of the city."

26
00:01:49.552 --> 00:01:55.494
"John Canty is not my father, and I've never begged a day in my life."

27
00:01:57.675 --> 00:01:58.295
"Listen to me."

28
00:01:59.076 --> 00:02:00.216
Frank was angry now.

29
00:02:01.512 --> 00:02:06.353
"Since you're too good to beg or steal, you'll play decoy while I beg.

30
00:02:06.713 --> 00:02:07.074
Got it?"

31
00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.875
Edward was about to argue again when Frank hushed him.

32
00:02:10.895 --> 00:02:13.535
"Here comes a man with a kind face.

33
00:02:15.436 --> 00:02:18.677
First I'll pretend I'm sick, and then you call out to him."

34
00:02:19.917 --> 00:02:20.977
Edward gritted his teeth.

35
00:02:20.997 --> 00:02:24.298
"There's no way I'm taking part in your scheme."

36
00:02:26.119 --> 00:02:28.999
Frank pinched Edward's arm and snarled in his ear.

37
00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:35.223
"You say, 'Oh, kind sir, my poor brother is afflicted with a terrible illness, and we don't know

38
00:02:35.283 --> 00:02:35.903
anyone here.

39
00:02:37.144 --> 00:02:40.246
Please help us with just one penny from your great riches.'

40
00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:46.731
Understand?" Before Edward could refuse, Frank dropped to the ground in front of the man.

41
00:02:46.751 --> 00:02:49.413
"Oh dear, oh dear!"

42
00:02:49.853 --> 00:02:50.794
the stranger cried.

43
00:02:50.814 --> 00:02:52.955
"What's wrong?

44
00:02:53.396 --> 00:02:54.216
Let me help you!"

45
00:02:54.236 --> 00:02:59.140
"I don't want to trouble you with my illness," Frank said.

46
00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:05.322
"My brother will tell you that I'm often sick and racked with pain.

47
00:03:06.422 --> 00:03:10.804
All I ask is a penny for food, and then leave me to my misery."

48
00:03:10.824 --> 00:03:12.785
"A penny?

49
00:03:13.365 --> 00:03:14.886
I'll give you three pennies!"

50
00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:19.888
The man fumbled in his pocket and handed the coins to Frank.

51
00:03:19.908 --> 00:03:28.252
"Now come here, lad, and help me carry your brother to the house—" "I'm not his brother," Edward

52
00:03:28.312 --> 00:03:33.666
interrupted. "Oh, he denies knowing his own brother."

53
00:03:35.468 --> 00:03:37.589
Frank groaned as the man bent over him.

54
00:03:37.609 --> 00:03:40.731
"We are both sick.

55
00:03:41.912 --> 00:03:46.335
While my illness destroys my body, his sickness eats away his mind."

56
00:03:48.797 --> 00:03:52.559
The stranger looked suspiciously from Edward to Frank and back again.

57
00:03:52.579 --> 00:03:59.224
"If he's not your brother," the man said to Edward, "then who is he?"

58
00:04:00.428 --> 00:04:01.549
"A beggar and a thief.

59
00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:07.252
While you've been giving him pennies, he's been picking your pocket!"

60
00:04:08.432 --> 00:04:12.214
The man's eyes widened in surprise, and he patted his empty pocket.

61
00:04:13.655 --> 00:04:16.577
Frank jumped up and ran away with the man in hot pursuit.

62
00:04:17.597 --> 00:04:20.899
Without wasting a second, Edward fled in the opposite direction.

63
00:04:20.919 --> 00:04:24.821
"Expecting the king to beg and steal.

64
00:04:25.121 --> 00:04:30.004
Ridiculous!" Edward kept looking back for Frank as he hurried along.

65
00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:38.463
However, as the hours passed and he grew hungry, Edward realized that he'd have to beg for food.

66
00:04:42.265 --> 00:04:46.728
He knocked on a farmhouse door, but the owner took one look at his ragged clothes and shooed

67
00:04:46.768 --> 00:04:47.208
him away.

68
00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:52.010
can manage on my own!

69
00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:54.772
I don't need anybody's charity!"

70
00:04:55.212 --> 00:04:57.834
Edward shouted as he walked down the farmhouse lane.

71
00:04:59.455 --> 00:05:01.816
A cow raised its head and stared after him.

72
00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.342
Night arrived with a damp chill.

73
00:05:07.623 --> 00:05:12.807
Edward was tired, but every time he sat down to rest, the cold penetrated his bones.

74
00:05:12.827 --> 00:05:17.531
"I have to find somewhere warm to spend the night."

75
00:05:19.073 --> 00:05:21.095
He got up and started walking again.

76
00:05:23.697 --> 00:05:27.760
At last he came to a barn, where a farmworker was finishing some chores.

77
00:05:29.182 --> 00:05:31.544
Edward waited outside, near the open door.

78
00:05:32.844 --> 00:05:37.587
By the light of the man's lantern, he spotted an empty stall and some horse blankets.

79
00:05:39.269 --> 00:05:40.369
"There's my bed!"

80
00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:41.610
Edward thought.

81
00:05:44.833 --> 00:05:48.175
As soon as the man left, Edward crept into the dark barn.

82
00:05:49.796 --> 00:05:54.339
He put one blanket on the ground, lay down, and pulled the other blanket over him.

83
00:05:54.359 --> 00:06:00.284
"Ugh! These blankets stink of horse, but they'll have to do."

84
00:06:02.596 --> 00:06:05.699
Edward was almost asleep when something touched his face.

85
00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:08.461
He sat up in alarm.

86
00:06:08.481 --> 00:06:09.982
"Who's there?"

87
00:06:10.222 --> 00:06:10.842
he whispered.

88
00:06:12.103 --> 00:06:13.104
No one replied.

89
00:06:14.585 --> 00:06:18.348
Edward lay down with his eyes wide open even though it was too dark to see.

90
00:06:18.368 --> 00:06:22.751
The thing reached out and touched him again!
